title: $:/plugins/nikorion/pkm-schema/fields/priority
tags: $:/tags/nikorion/pkm/Field
kind: vocab
list: 2 1 0
applies-filter: [<currentTiddler>get[role]match[task]] [<currentTiddler>get[role]match[tasklist]] [<currentTiddler>get[role]match[routine]] [<currentTiddler>!has[role]]
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

One value from the vocabulary in `list`, in display order: `2` high, `1` normal, `0` low. The slugs are digits so that sorting on the field orders by urgency — as text or as numbers alike —, which is also why there is no blank value: an empty `normal` would sort apart from `1`. A piece of work with no priority is one nobody has rated yet. List the urgent ones with `[priority[2]]`, the most urgent first with `[has[priority]!sort[priority]]`.

Same `applies-filter` as `status`, and for the same reason: only a piece of work has a priority. Keep the two in step, and `Field/priority/Applies` in each language.
